{"id": 75, "ts": 1780592777.9950662, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the stronger overall fit.\u202fJames confirmed we have no direct observation of B\u2019s decision\u2011making under pressure, but his record of handling stress very well and being very conscientious strongly suggests he can make sound, timely judgments when the cockpit gets demanding.\u202fCombined with his proven ability to assess weather conditions and his excellent computer skills\u2014critical for long\u2011haul navigation and systems management\u2014B meets the core technical and stress\u2011resilience criteria.\nBy contrast, Candidate\u202fC does demonstrate quick, correct decisions and a calm crisis demeanor, and he creates a positive crew atmosphere. However, his unwillingness to pursue further education and the note that he is \u201cregarded as egocentric\u201d raise serious doubts about his adaptability and long\u2011term growth in a constantly evolving regulatory and technological environment.\u202fHis difficulty communicating ideas also risks crew coordination, even if his overall attitude toward others is positive.\nGiven B\u2019s solid reliability, stress handling, and technical competence, and considering that his communication and numeric\u2011memory concerns can be mitigated through targeted training, I keep my vote for Candidate\u202fB."}
