{"id": 79, "ts": 1780592827.2305365, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I concur with Emily\u2019s assessment and keep my provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fB.\u202fWhile James rightly points out we lack a direct observation of B\u2019s decision\u2011making under pressure, his documented strengths\u2014very conscientious, handles stress very well, excels at weather assessment and computer\u2011based navigation\u2014directly support the core technical and stress\u2011resilience criteria for long\u2011haul operations.\u202fThe concerns about B\u2019s grumpiness, occasional uncooperativeness, and a weak memory for numbers are real, but they are specific, observable behaviours that can be addressed through targeted crew\u2011resource\u2011training and procedural checks.\u202fBy contrast, Candidate\u202fC, although 100\u202f% reliable and calm in crises, shows a reluctance to further his education and is described as egocentric, which raises deeper doubts about his adaptability and long\u2011term growth in our evolving regulatory environment.\u202fGiven the balance of evidence, B remains the strongest overall fit at this stage, pending any new data on A or D."}
