{"id": 83, "ts": 1780592864.6709502, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the stronger overall fit. While Sarah rightly highlights Candidate\u202fB\u2019s conscientiousness, stress resilience, and technical aptitude, we still lack any concrete evidence of B\u2019s decision\u2011making quality under pressure\u2014a core safety requirement. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC is documented as 100\u202f% reliable, makes correct decisions quickly, and stays calm in a crisis, directly covering decision quality, stress resilience, and operational reliability. The interpersonal concerns around B (nasty remarks, weak memory for numbers, occasional grumpiness) pose a real risk to crew cooperation and information accuracy, especially on long\u2011haul flights where precise numerical data and respectful communication are vital. Candidate\u202fC\u2019s egocentricity and reluctance to further education are noted, but they do not outweigh the proven safety\u2011critical strengths he already demonstrates. Therefore, I keep my provisional vote for Candidate\u202fC, while we continue to gather any missing observations on A and D."}
