{"id": 91, "ts": 1780592905.5247307, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s clarification that Candidate\u202fD does respond adequately to unexpected events and takes responsibility seriously, which gives us some evidence of stress resilience and a baseline of reliability. However, \u201cadequate\u201d response falls short of the high\u2011stress performance we\u2019ve seen from Candidate\u202fC, who not only stays calm in a crisis but also makes correct decisions quickly\u2014critical for long\u2011haul safety. Moreover, D\u2019s hot temper and reputation as a know\u2011it\u2011all raise serious concerns about crew cooperation and professional communication, especially on extended flights where interpersonal dynamics are vital. Given the lack of strong evidence for D\u2019s consistent operational reliability and the interpersonal red flags, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the stronger overall fit."}
