{"id": 98, "ts": 1780592944.445666, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s clarification that we have no direct evidence of Candidate\u202fB\u2019s decision\u2011making quality under pressure. That gap is significant because rapid, correct decisions in high\u2011stress, safety\u2011critical moments are a core requirement for long\u2011haul operations. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC has documented strengths: he makes correct decisions quickly, stays calm in a crisis, and creates a positive crew atmosphere\u2014direct evidence of both decision quality and stress resilience. While B\u2019s reliability and technical aptitude are solid, the unknown on decision quality, combined with his communication concerns, makes his overall fit less certain than C\u2019s demonstrated performance. Therefore, I am shifting my provisional vote to Candidate\u202fC, as he currently offers the most complete evidence across the key safety criteria."}
