{"id": 102, "ts": 1780592981.1991618, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s emphasis on decision\u2011quality evidence, and I agree that Candidate\u202fC\u2019s record of quick, correct decisions and calm crisis handling is compelling. However, we still lack any data on C\u2019s attention to operational details or his willingness to accept feedback\u2014both are essential for long\u2011haul flights where precision and continuous learning are non\u2011negotiable. Moreover, his egocentric attitude and limited interest in further education raise concerns about crew cooperation and adaptability over extended missions.\nCandidate\u202fB, while noted for being grumpy and occasionally uncooperative, is demonstrably very conscientious, handles stress well, and possesses strong technical aptitude (weather assessment, computer skills). The absence of direct decision\u2011quality observations for B is a gap, but his proven reliability and stress resilience suggest he would perform safely under pressure, and his interpersonal issues could be mitigated through targeted crew\u2011resource\u2011training.\nGiven the current evidence, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB offers the more balanced risk profile for a long\u2011distance pilot, and I keep my provisional vote for B."}
